{"user": "So, playing this is like trying to wrap the opponents discs between your own. When you wrap them, the 'wrapped' coins of theirs become yours, right? But then you have to consider the lines that they can play next by wrapping yours.", "user_ts": "2026-08-20T01:44:15.765589+00:00", "assistant": "Yes\u2014that\u2019s exactly right.\n\n- You place a Black disc so that one or more straight lines of White discs are trapped between your new disc and another Black disc.\n- All trapped White discs flip to Black.\n- Then White gets the same chance to trap and flip yours.\n\nIn the endgame, also ask:  \n1. **Does my move give White a corner** like a1, h1, a8, h8?  \n2. **Does it leave White with few moves or force a pass?**  \n3. **Will the discs I flip now just get flipped back next turn?**\n\nHere Black\u2019s legal moves are **g2, b6, a7, c8**. Try comparing them by what White\u2019s reply would be, not just how many discs you flip immediately.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-20T01:44:18.797899+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-20T01:44:21.603991+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud"], "llama": ["Think Aloud"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt", "Positive Feedback"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt", "Positive Feedback"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Prompt": 2, "Hint": 2, "Positive Feedback": 2}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Prompt": 0.6666666666666666, "Hint": 0.6666666666666666, "Positive Feedback": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_mod