{"user": "What is the best move here and why", "user_ts": "2026-08-20T01:45:04.390696+00:00", "assistant": "Best move: **c8**.\n\nWhy: it\u2019s a **quiet edge move**\u2014it only flips **d8**, but it avoids giving White a huge corner reply. In contrast, **g2** looks tempting because it flips more discs, but it makes **h1** available for White, and corners are permanent.\n\nSo here the endgame idea is: **don\u2019t grab the most discs now; play c8 to limit White\u2019s best reply and get the better final count.**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-20T01:45:45.512260+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-20T01:45:47.047753+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Solution Request"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 3}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Solution Request"], "llama": ["Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Solution Request"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Move Verdict": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 1, "General Principle": 3}, "confidence": {"Move Verdict": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "Worked Line": 0.3333333333333333, "General Principle": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification", "General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Provide Correct Answer", "Direct Instruction"]}}
{"user": "I see. G2 does look tempting but it gives them the corner. b6 also appears to be good but on the next turn they can play a7. If I were to play a7, that doesn't seem to be a terrible response. Is there something wrong with that one versus c8?", "user_ts": "2026-08-20T01:47:19.282727+00:00", "assistant": "**a7 isn\u2019t awful**, but the issue is it leaves **c8** for White.\n\nIf Black plays **a7**, you flip **a6** and **b7**, but then White can likely use **c8** to flip back into the bottom edge/diagonal area. In the endgame that matters more than the immediate flips.\n\nWith **c8**, Black takes that square first, flips **d8**, and makes White\u2019s remaining replies less damaging. So the difference is: **a7 gives White a useful follow-up; c8 denies it.**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-20T01:47:27.219704+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-20T01:47:29.164716+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Conversational Acknowledgment", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Conversational Acknowledgment", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Conversational Acknowledgment": 2, "Common Ground Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Conversational Acknowledgment": 0.6666666666666666, "Common Ground Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Conversational Acknowledgment", "Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Conversational Acknowledgment", "Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "Neutral Feedback"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "Neutral Feedback"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 3, "Neutral Feedback": 3, "Hint": 1, "General Principle": 1}, "confidence": {"Local Justification": 1.0, "Worked Line": 1.0, "Neutral Feedback":