{"user": "I see. It is quite difficult to calculate these things.", "user_ts": "2026-08-20T01:48:32.660950+00:00", "assistant": "Yes\u2014endgames are hard because the \u201cbest-looking\u201d move can lose after 2\u20133 forced replies.\n\nA useful shortcut here:\n\n- **Corners first:** avoid giving White **h1** or **a8**.\n- **Deny key moves:** ask \u201cwhat important square am I leaving White?\u201d\n- **Count stable discs, not flips:** edge/corner discs matter more than middle flips.\n\nIn this position, the main comparison is whether your move gives White a strong follow-up like **c8** or a corner access.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-20T01:48:33.607752+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-20T01:48:35.549537+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Metacomment"], "consensus": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Metacomment"], "votes": {"Conversational Acknowledgment": 3, "Metacomment": 2, "Think Aloud": 1}, "confidence": {"Conversational Acknowledgment": 1.0, "Metacomment": 0.6666666666666666, "Think Aloud": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Metacomment"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Conversational Acknowledgment"], "sonnet": ["Conversational Acknowledgment", "Metacomment"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle", "Hint"], "consensus": ["General Principle", "Hint"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Hint": 3, "Local Justification": 1}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Hint": 1.0, "Local Justification": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle", "Hint"], "llama": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Hint"], "sonnet": ["General Principle", "Hint"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint"]}}
